{
  "The Bell Tower": "El Campanario",
  "Test Field": "Campo de pruebas",
  "A page": "",
  "A page, half buried in the grass.": "",
  "Notice board": "",
  "Nothing pinned here is worth reading yet.": "",
  "Chest": "",
  "Inside: a little bread, wrapped in cloth.": "",
  "Art Yard": "Patio de arte",
  "The Greenmarch": "La Marca Verde",
  "Soldiers behind the barricade: \"Nobody goes through to Ashford until the Steward says so.\" Bring the Steward news from the north worth hearing, and the road will open. (Later in the story.)": "",
  "A rockfall blocks the hill path to the Greyfang Hills. It will take more than one pair of hands to clear. (Later in the story.)": "",
  "The Hollow King's proclamation": "La proclama del Rey Hueco",
  "A proclamation, nailed up over the old notices. It is in your journal now (J).": "",
  "The hollow in the old oak": "",
  "A hollow in the old oak, dark and dry. Nothing in it you can see from here.": "",
  "Inside the hollow, wrapped in a Warden's oilskin: a key to a code of feathers, two notes signed V., and on top of them a black crow feather, fresh as this morning. (J)": "",
  "Heron Lodge": "Pabellón de la Garza",
  "The hearth": "",
  "A big stone hearth, cold since the Wardens were sent home. Three logs would light it.": "",
  "You lay the fire and light it. For the first time in seven years, there is smoke over Heron Lodge.": "",
  "The roll of the Wardens": "La lista de los Guardianes",
  "Names, cut into the beam over the hearth. Too dark to read without a fire.": "",
  "A Warden's chest": "",
  "In the Warden's chest: bandages, a tinderbox gone to rust, and a ration of smoked meat sealed in wax.": "",
  "The weapon rack": "",
  "Two old spears. The good blades went with the Wardens when they were sent home.": "",
  "Someone has cut the shape of a feather into this stump, long ago. It means nothing to you.": "",
  "A Warden cache": "",
  "An owl scratched on a mossy stone. Somebody meant something by it.": "",
  "Under the owl mark at {0}, wrapped in oilskin: a Warden's cache, still dry.": "",
  "Heron Reach": "Recodo de la Garza",
  "Grave-mist stands across the road like a wall. Walk into it and you come out where you went in. Without a trail to follow, nobody gets through. (Follow the Warden marks.)": "",
  "A feather cut in the bark": "",
  "An owl, cut over Heron Lodge's door. \"Shelter.\" He recut it the spring he went.": "",
  "A heron, at the ford. \"The water. The crossing.\"": "",
  "A goose cut over a heron. \"Onward, to the crossing.\" Wren touches it, and the grave-mist across the road begins to thin.": "",
  "the split oak": "",
  "the old weir": "",
  "the leaning stone": "",
  "A page caught on the thorns": "",
  "A scrap of paper flaps on the thorns, too high and too tangled to bother with. Someone might want it, though.": "",
  "A page, caught on a bone spike over the river. Her hand. Nan will want it.": "",
  "A letter on the lodge's step": "",
  "A letter on Heron Lodge's step, addressed to the King at Castle Corvane. The wrong door, by a long way. (J)": "",
  "The Wardens' fire-ring": "",
  "A ring of stones at the barrow door, the ash in it seven years cold. Not while whatever pushed the door stone out is still awake in there.": "",
  "You lay three logs in the old ring and light them. \"We keep the fire, so others may sleep.\" Somewhere under the hill, something settles.": "",
  "You wake by the hearth in Heron Lodge, under forty names.": "",
  "You wake on a bench by Mother Dunn's fire. Someone has put a blanket over you.": "",
  "The King's Chase": "El Coto del Rey",
  "A wall of thornwood and bones, goblin-built, closes the hill path east. The spikes point outward, toward the hills. Whatever the goblins built it against, it's on the other side. (Act III.)": "",
  "The King's game book": "El libro de caza del Rey",
  "On the table by the lodge door, under a fallen rafter: the foresters' game book. It is in your journal now. (J)": "",
  "The kennels": "",
  "Every pen empty, every door gnawed open from the inside. Wren will want to see this.": "",
  "A rope on the Gallows Willow": "",
  "A frayed rope hangs from the low branch, creaking, though there is no wind.": "",
  "You cut the rope down. It falls in a heap, stiff as wire.": "",
  "Tam Pell's rope": "",
  "The rope nearest the trunk. Grandad Pell would want to know.": "",
  "You cut Tam Pell down, last of all, and bury him under the willow where the Ride bends. It is not much of a grave. It is more than he had.": "",
  "Pike's courier": "",
  "Something lies in the long grass by the Ride. Wolves have been at it.": "",
  "Under the hedge by the Ride, what the wolves left of the Steward's courier. His satchel is gone. Wolf tracks and goblin boots lead east, toward the outriders' camp.": "",
  "You wake by Wren's fire. She doesn't look up. \"You snore.\"": "",
  "The Lisle Barrow": "El Túmulo del Lisle",
  "Millbrook": "Millbrook",
  "Black thorns as thick as your arm close the north road. The Lisle runs under them, off to the west.": "",
  "The Lisle runs under the thorn wall here, under a low arch of black stems. There might be a way through along the bank, for someone who knew it.": "",
  "The tower door is locked. Father Odo keeps the key.": "",
  "The herald's board": "",
  "The Steward's bounty, nailed up beside the Hollow King's proclamation. You take a notice. (J)": "",
  "Black thorn shoots": "",
  "Black thorns, pushing up through the crops. Cold to the touch. Someone in the village might know what to do about them.": "",
  "You set the shoots alight. They burn slow and cold, hissing like breath, and leave a black thorn in the ash.": "",
  "A letter on the doorstep": "",
  "A letter, sealed, lying on the step. The grey postman's footprints lead away into the dark, and simply stop.": "",
  "A letter on the mill step": "",
  "A letter on the mill step, addressed to Nan. The wrong door: hers is further along. (J)": "",
  "The grey postman turns his blank face toward you, and is gone like breath off a window. Whatever he is, steel can't reach him. Not yet.": "",
  "The Weeping Bridge": "El Puente Llorón",
  "Past the bridge, black vines as thick as a man choke the road north, and they move when you look away. Fire only makes them angry. (Act III.)": "",
  "The King's post": "",
  "A proclamation, nailed to the post at the end of the bridge. It is in your journal now. (J)": "",
  "A page on the thorns by the road, the ink run with mist. Her hand. Nan will want it.": "",
  "The Weepwood": "El Bosque Llorón",
  "The thorns that close Millbrook's north road. Wren's river path, to the west, goes under them.": "",
  "A black willow has come down across the road, thorns as long as swords. Fire won't take it and an axe bounces off. The charcoal-burners at Kilnholt have a two-man saw. (Help Kilnholt, and they'll clear it.)": "",
  "Wren's fire": "",
  "A ring of stones where Wren's fire was, long cold. Two logs would get it going again.": "",
  "You build the fire up and it catches. Wren holds her hands to it and says nothing, which from Wren is a thank-you.": "",
  "A grey goose, cut into the bark by Wren's camp. \"Onward. Up the river.\" He started his round here.": "",
  "A jay, at the edge of the spider dell. \"Danger: go round.\" He recut it the spring he went.": "",
  "A goose on the old road above Kilnholt. \"Onward.\" North, toward the river.": "",
  "You work the page free of the thorns without tearing it. Her hand. Nan will want it.": "",
  "A page, snagged on a thorn over an unmarked grave. Her hand again. Nan will want it.": "",
  "A cocoon": "",
  "You slit the silk. Inside, what's left of a traveller, and his pack: bandages, a few coins and a skein of silk.": "",
  "Grey dust": "",
  "Where the lantern went out there are no footprints. Only grey dust, and a dead moth as big as your hand. (J)": "",
  "Dawn. The dead lie down where they stand and are only soot again. Five kilns or more still burn: the ring held.": "",
  "Dawn, and too many kilns have gone cold. Hesketh says nothing. The burners light them again, and wait for another night.": "",
  "The lantern is gone.": "",
  "black willow": "",
  "black oak": ""
}
